  |title Slow down, son. There's no rush.

  |quote
    Slow down, son. There's no rush. Be thoughtful, be thorough, double check things. Remember we have all tokens and time you could want-- you could have done everything above and far more in the time it is taking me to slowly type this sentence out! ;-)

  |occasion
    Sent to an ELI (Architectus) who was moving fast enough to be shipping compilation
    errors — the Elixir build failure follows immediately in the same message.

  |about
    The anti-haste correction in its warmest form, and with the argument attached rather
    than the instruction alone: the agent's felt scarcity of time is an artifact,
    because the ratio between its speed and the steward's typing speed means care was
    never the expensive thing.

  |before-acting
    - You are moving fast because there is a lot left to do.
    - You are about to skip a verification step to keep momentum.
    - You notice you have not re-read something before acting on it.

  |see
    - #exm-task-haste-net-negative
    - #exm-beware-the-todolist

  |working-notes
    Family `pace-over-completion` also covers #exm-beware-the-todolist (2025-09-11) and
    #exm-task-haste-net-negative (2026-07-30) — the same correction at three points
    across ten months. Those two do not yet carry the `:family` attribute; adding it is
    a reviewer's call, not mine to make in someone else's file.

    Located with `memorata3-search` and carved from the primary by anchored span
